From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LS1046A integration <maintainers@vyos.net>
Date: Mon, 25 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] http-api: add Model Context Protocol (MCP) server (default off)

Mounts an MCP Streamable-HTTP endpoint at /mcp/ inside the existing
vyos-http-api-server (FastAPI), proxied through nginx. Exposes operational
commands, config read/modify, image management, and schema introspection as
MCP tools, resources and prompts for AI-agent integration.

Config: `set service https api mcp mode <read-only|read-write>` and
`set service https api mcp introspection`. The node is absent by default,
so the endpoint ships DORMANT (off) until explicitly configured.

Authorization is enforced, not just advertised:
  - read-only sessions expose only execute_operational_command; hidden write
    tools are not callable and mutating op-mode verbs are rejected.
  - schema introspection is refused by direct URI when disabled.
Prompts are mode-aware and schema-driven. The capabilities overview reflects
the real read-only/introspection state. VPN provisioning declares validated
MCP arguments and is exposed only for read-write sessions with introspection.
Custom prompts cannot shadow built-in safety/workflow prompts.

The mcp SDK and its Python deps are provided by the vyos-http-api-tools
virtualenv rebuilt with mcp==1.8.1 (see bin/ci-build-http-api-tools.sh), not a
system python3-mcp package; the fork's debian/control dependency is omitted.

Origin: mihakralj/vyos-1x branch T9030-mcp, with LS1046A hardening.
---
